WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:02.202
I'm in the house I grew up in,

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.448
in the middle of Fife Scotland.

00:00:03.448 --> 00:00:05.892
There's no rational or logical explanation

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:06.979
(laughs)

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:08.309
or any reasonable idea for me to ever

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:11.549
have believed that I'd ever
get to perform on Conan.

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:12.629
And so every time I go, I'm like

00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:15.415
"They've made the same mistake
again, this is excellent.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.131
"Let's keep it turning up"

00:00:17.131 --> 00:00:18.689
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:19.956
[JP Buck] A lot of work goes into

00:00:19.956 --> 00:00:21.824
a short, late night stand-up set.

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:23.326
Join me, JP Buck as I spotlight

00:00:23.326 --> 00:00:24.646
the comedians who came up with

00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:27.065
some of my favorite comedy sets.

00:00:27.065 --> 00:00:28.565
This is The SetUp.

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:31.606
[Narrator] Please welcome
the very funny, Daniel Sloss.

00:00:31.606 --> 00:00:34.625
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:36.265
First time I heard about
you was at the Fringe

00:00:36.265 --> 00:00:38.023
and I didn't get to see you that year,

00:00:38.023 --> 00:00:41.574
but I was contacted by your
agent and you were going to

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.545
potentially be traveling to the U S.

00:00:44.545 --> 00:00:47.796
And so I, without ever having met you,

00:00:47.796 --> 00:00:50.324
helped set up a bunch of gigs for you.

00:00:50.324 --> 00:00:52.166
I don't know how much you know about this.

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:53.505
And then you actually had to cancel

00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:54.566
and you couldn't come over.

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:56.865
I don't know much of that.

00:00:56.865 --> 00:00:58.601
Yeah, I think I booked
at like the Ice House

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.033
and a bunch of other spots.

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:01.394
Why did I cancel?

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.574
Some scheduling issue.

00:01:02.574 --> 00:01:04.265
Believe me I was never offended by it.

00:01:04.265 --> 00:01:06.834
But the funny thing is
in order to see you,

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.134
I couldn't just drive to
Pasadena. I had to get on a plane,

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:11.796
fly to Edinburgh, see you at the Fringe.

00:01:11.796 --> 00:01:13.185
And not only get to Edinburgh.

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:14.633
Like, Edinburgh is, you know,

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:17.081
it's a long trip, but staying
at the center of town,

00:01:17.081 --> 00:01:20.974
most of the comedy shows
are at this other venue,

00:01:20.974 --> 00:01:23.442
different venues that are
pretty close to each other.

00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:25.345
Like there's the Pleasance
and there's the Underbelly.

00:01:25.345 --> 00:01:27.235
And there's the Leith.
The Harp, yeah

00:01:27.235 --> 00:01:28.068
they are all in the same area

00:01:28.068 --> 00:01:28.901
The Harp, yeah, yeah

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:29.734
Yeah, yeah

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:34.155
You choose to be another
25 minutes away of a walk

00:01:34.155 --> 00:01:36.014
away from those venues.

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:36.847
Yeah.

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:38.985
I land, and then I've
got to walk 25 minutes

00:01:38.985 --> 00:01:41.303
out of town to come see you.

00:01:41.303 --> 00:01:43.035
You gotta want me baby, you gotta want me

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:45.285
(laughing)

00:01:46.163 --> 00:01:48.043
Getting there was totally worth the trip.

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:49.563
It was one of the best
shows I had seen that year.

00:01:49.563 --> 00:01:51.115
And I, that night we were like,

00:01:51.115 --> 00:01:52.674
let's just figure out a set and do it.

00:01:52.674 --> 00:01:54.635
(music playing)

00:01:54.635 --> 00:01:56.053
Explain how you put your set together

00:01:56.053 --> 00:01:56.923
and what you sent me.

00:01:56.923 --> 00:01:58.494
That I just walk around the hotel room

00:01:58.494 --> 00:02:00.395
and recorded it to you there.

00:02:00.395 --> 00:02:01.228
Yeah.

00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:02.061
Oh God.

00:02:02.061 --> 00:02:03.123
Like a sociopath.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:06.154
(music playing)

00:02:06.154 --> 00:02:07.035
Older material.

00:02:07.035 --> 00:02:09.985
I really struggle to watch
myself any old shows of mine

00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:12.465
because I dunno. I just think I'm crap.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.809
Not then, just by comparison.

00:02:14.809 --> 00:02:17.545
So I watched this earlier and
I managed to get most of my

00:02:17.545 --> 00:02:19.216
cringing out.

00:02:19.216 --> 00:02:20.171
(music playing)

00:02:20.171 --> 00:02:21.921
For colleagues who haven't done TV before

00:02:21.921 --> 00:02:23.950
I say dress slightly better.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.219
You don't have to wear a suit,

00:02:25.219 --> 00:02:26.538
but slightly better than
what you would wear on stage.

00:02:26.538 --> 00:02:27.819
This is slightly better

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:32.236
than what I wear on stage (laughing)

00:02:33.661 --> 00:02:34.950
Hello.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:35.990
[Audience] Hello

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.061
Are we all doing oh well?

00:02:37.061 --> 00:02:38.140
[Audience] Yes

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.150
Most of us fairly
disappointed that a child

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.571
just walked on stage.

00:02:40.571 --> 00:02:42.561
(audience laughing)

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:43.782
(clapping)

00:02:43.782 --> 00:02:44.769
(audience laughing)

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:46.510
I didn't even like Home Alone, damn.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.399
(audience laughing)

00:02:48.399 --> 00:02:51.150
This was the cut-off point
for that joke working, right.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.921
I'd been doing that joke
since I was 17 years old.

00:02:53.921 --> 00:02:55.790
And in this I'm 23.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.079
I was really stretching the child

00:02:58.079 --> 00:03:02.171
last drops of the milker
that we're just going, okay.

00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:03.004
And I guess I still, you
look, look young there.

00:03:03.004 --> 00:03:06.254
(upbeat music playing)

00:03:08.539 --> 00:03:09.771
My mom's had four kids.

00:03:09.771 --> 00:03:11.550
You can tell that she
loves us all the same,

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.259
but after the first two,
she kind of stopped caring.

00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:17.291
She'll always go on about,
how she was blessed with me.

00:03:17.291 --> 00:03:19.679
Then she was gifted with my sister.

00:03:19.679 --> 00:03:21.670
Then she had my brother

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:22.790
(audience laughing)

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:23.889
and she'll always remember the day

00:03:23.889 --> 00:03:25.678
that she was diagnosed with the other one.

00:03:25.678 --> 00:03:27.347
We need to stop right there.

00:03:27.347 --> 00:03:28.686
(laughing)

00:03:28.686 --> 00:03:33.466
I'm so excited. I put that
joke in there specifically,

00:03:33.466 --> 00:03:34.508
the joke that's about to happen.

00:03:34.508 --> 00:03:38.079
I put it in there specifically
because I knew that you were

00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:39.136
gonna take it out.

00:03:39.136 --> 00:03:41.296
It's a joke that I put in every single set

00:03:41.296 --> 00:03:42.527
throughout the years because I know

00:03:42.527 --> 00:03:43.839
especially the UK

00:03:43.839 --> 00:03:45.948
people wanna edit your set

00:03:45.948 --> 00:03:47.468
just so they feel that
you've edited your set.

00:03:47.468 --> 00:03:49.199
So you put in something that you know,

00:03:49.199 --> 00:03:50.748
is not going to get in.

00:03:50.748 --> 00:03:53.895
They take it out, they feel
like they've done their job.

00:03:53.895 --> 00:03:56.047
And then they leave the
rest of the set alone.

00:03:56.047 --> 00:03:58.607
That is purely the reason
I put that joke in the set.

00:03:58.607 --> 00:04:01.508
And you were the first person
when I sent through this set

00:04:01.508 --> 00:04:02.341
you were like

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.174
"Yeah, I'll fight for it."

00:04:03.174 --> 00:04:04.007
And I was like

00:04:04.007 --> 00:04:05.146
"There's no way

00:04:05.146 --> 00:04:05.979
(laughing)

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.519
"There's now way this is
gonna be on the show."

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:12.382
When you said I could,
genuinely, watching it,

00:04:12.382 --> 00:04:13.215
watching this clip

00:04:13.215 --> 00:04:16.818
the joy on my face, the sheer joy.

00:04:16.818 --> 00:04:18.707
And it's a genuine laugh.

00:04:18.707 --> 00:04:20.148
And it's such a genuine reaction

00:04:20.148 --> 00:04:21.367
of a mischievous child going

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.737
(giggles)

00:04:22.737 --> 00:04:24.527
I can't believe they let me do it.

00:04:24.527 --> 00:04:26.927
We were all intentional
though, which is good.

00:04:26.927 --> 00:04:29.536
My mom has a very healthy
outlook to contraception,

00:04:29.536 --> 00:04:33.245
which is great because her
sister is anti-abortion,

00:04:33.245 --> 00:04:35.458
which is a cruel nickname,
but she's had five.

00:04:35.458 --> 00:04:39.234
(audience laughing)

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.668
I'm as surprised as you are
that they let me do that joke.

00:04:41.668 --> 00:04:43.656
I (laughing)

00:04:43.656 --> 00:04:46.195
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:04:46.195 --> 00:04:49.258
He Keeps going, hold on, just a laugh

00:04:49.258 --> 00:04:51.448
(laughs)

00:04:51.448 --> 00:04:52.690
I know, I'm shocked.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.177
(audience laughing)

00:04:54.177 --> 00:04:57.858
But that's the moment
where I properly relaxed.

00:04:57.858 --> 00:05:01.247
That was just, I can't,
I still can't believe,

00:05:01.247 --> 00:05:06.080
I got to tell that joke on
national television in America.

00:05:07.781 --> 00:05:08.731
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:05:08.731 --> 00:05:09.564
That was great.

00:05:09.564 --> 00:05:10.597
Thank you man

00:05:10.597 --> 00:05:11.430
That was fantastic.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.263
I enjoyed it.

00:05:12.263 --> 00:05:15.236
Daniel Sloss, ladies and
gentlemen, really nice job.

00:05:15.236 --> 00:05:16.327
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:18.236
The comment from everyone
was the exact same,

00:05:18.236 --> 00:05:20.386
which is when you watch
Gordon coming up to me,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:24.791
it seems like he's genuinely
surprised that I was good.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:25.764
Like, he's like,

00:05:25.764 --> 00:05:29.434
"That was great. Oh my God,
it's good. The child was funny."

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.975
And that it's just me star struck

00:05:31.975 --> 00:05:33.623
and bumbling through words like.

00:05:33.623 --> 00:05:35.874
"I had a lot of fun.
Thanks for having me."

00:05:35.874 --> 00:05:38.994
(upbeat music playing)

00:05:38.994 --> 00:05:40.604
One of the kind of ongoing discussions

00:05:40.604 --> 00:05:41.823
in the comment section

00:05:41.823 --> 00:05:45.153
was your level of attractiveness.

00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:46.560
Is it? Really?

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.393
No.

00:05:47.393 --> 00:05:48.226
Is it?

00:05:48.226 --> 00:05:49.059
Yeah, hell yeah, yeah.

00:05:49.059 --> 00:05:49.999
I mean, there's one that's right here

00:05:49.999 --> 00:05:50.832
It says

00:05:50.832 --> 00:05:52.433
"He is probably one of
the hottest comedians

00:05:52.433 --> 00:05:53.441
"I've ever seen."

00:05:53.441 --> 00:05:54.505
Exclamation point.

00:05:54.505 --> 00:05:56.327
I don't read YouTube comments

00:05:56.327 --> 00:05:57.765
because I used to read YouTube

00:05:57.765 --> 00:06:00.015
comments all the time and, and, and they,

00:06:00.015 --> 00:06:01.204
they hurt my feelings. So I was like,

00:06:01.204 --> 00:06:02.535
I'll just not do that again.

00:06:02.535 --> 00:06:04.375
But now that there's a full on discussion

00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:08.875
about how attractive I am
maybe I'll get back into it.

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:12.265
You were like, would
you like to do it again?

00:06:12.265 --> 00:06:13.985
And that's just something people say,

00:06:13.985 --> 00:06:15.393
or I thought that was just something

00:06:15.393 --> 00:06:17.535
I thought that was your legal obligation

00:06:17.535 --> 00:06:18.368
to say that after the show

00:06:18.368 --> 00:06:19.201
you're like

00:06:19.201 --> 00:06:20.711
"Hey well, have you got any time?

00:06:20.711 --> 00:06:21.544
(laughing)

00:06:21.544 --> 00:06:22.443
"Next time you're in town."

00:06:22.443 --> 00:06:24.525
And then, yeah, it's just, I mean, for me,

00:06:24.525 --> 00:06:28.365
and I'd like to use this as
an opportunity to say this

00:06:28.365 --> 00:06:30.525
I've been doing this work,

00:06:30.525 --> 00:06:32.122
my first set was 2013, was it?

00:06:32.122 --> 00:06:33.543
December 2013?

00:06:33.543 --> 00:06:37.634
Conaco and Conan have been
so immensely supportive

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:38.772
over my career.

00:06:38.772 --> 00:06:39.605
Like the fact that,

00:06:39.605 --> 00:06:40.438
you know,

00:06:40.438 --> 00:06:44.277
you did take a small young
comedian from the other side of

00:06:44.277 --> 00:06:46.237
the world and you took a risk on them.

00:06:46.237 --> 00:06:49.615
You let them go on stage. Not
only did you, let me go on TV,

00:06:49.615 --> 00:06:51.685
you let me do the material
that I wanted to do.

00:06:51.685 --> 00:06:54.077
You really tried your
hardest to not edit it.

00:06:54.077 --> 00:06:56.776
And then everyone backstage,

00:06:56.776 --> 00:06:57.683
from the,

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.854
from the crew to the camera crew,

00:06:59.854 --> 00:07:00.987
to the runners,

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:03.765
and it's just a joy to do.

00:07:03.765 --> 00:07:06.197
And then every time I
go back, it's just, eh,

00:07:06.197 --> 00:07:08.216
it's something I never expected
the chance to get to do

00:07:08.216 --> 00:07:11.646
multiple times. And every time
I go back, it's just such a,

00:07:11.646 --> 00:07:13.463
I don't know, a home away
from home and a pleasure.

00:07:13.463 --> 00:07:14.747
So just thank you so much for ever

00:07:14.747 --> 00:07:17.375
allowing me to be part
of this insane thing.

00:07:17.375 --> 00:07:19.485
It's been, it's a pleasure for all of us

00:07:19.485 --> 00:07:20.827
and we love having you,

00:07:20.827 --> 00:07:21.660
and you're part of the family.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:22.885
Thanks again for doing this and

00:07:22.885 --> 00:07:24.296
can't wait to see you soon.

00:07:24.296 --> 00:07:25.576
Love to you all.

00:07:25.576 --> 00:07:28.076
Thank you all very, very much.

